        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomObject> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        ADDED 2026-08-20. Workstream B (disposition-tranche-2-requirements.md, D4.1/A7).
        Append-only history of broker replacements on a disposition BOV, one row per swap.
        This is the schema half only - BovSubmissionService.replaceSelectedBroker (D4.3) is
        the developer-owned writer and is out of scope for this deliverable.

        API NAME WAS AN OPEN NAMING ITEM (design O-1), NOW ACCEPTED: BOV_Broker_Change__c.
        Alternatives rejected: Broker_Replacement__c (ambiguous with Broker_Assignment__c's
        own "replace" concept), BOV_Broker_History__c ("History" collides with the platform's
        __History feature). This name follows ARCHITECTURE.md §1 (Title_Case_With_Underscores,
        no prefix, acronym fully uppercase).

        SETTINGS ARE COPIED FROM BOV_Submission__c.object-meta.xml, DELIBERATELY AND EXACTLY,
        matching every other disposition child object in this repo (Disposition_Offer__c,
        Broker_Listing__c, NDA__c, Wire__c): sharingModel/externalSharingModel Private (NOT
        the sf-custom-object skill's generic ReadWrite default - this object has no
        Master-Detail field, but the disposition module is uniformly Private OWD per the
        2026-07-22 RBAC build and every sibling child object matches it), enableHistory false,
        enableActivities false, enableReports true, enableSearch true, enableBulkApi true,
        deploymentStatus Deployed, visibility Public. AutoNumber name BBC-{0000}.

        🔴 FLS: EVERY FIELD ON THIS OBJECT ARRIVES WITH NO PERMISSIONS FOR ANYONE, SYSTEM
        ADMINISTRATOR INCLUDED.

        ⚠ CORRECTED 2026-08-20 (re-review, same day as C3 below). Retracted in place rather
        than silently edited, because the stale version described a grant this file's own C3
        fix exists specifically to remove - a future reader seeing `editable=false` a few
        fields below against a header still promising `read+edit` could reasonably conclude a
        PermissionSet's wholesale fieldPermissions replace (see the C3 note below) had
        accidentally DROPPED the edit grant, and "restore" it - silently UNDOING the fix that
        keeps this audit trail from being rewritable:

            RETRACTED: "Read is granted in DPEG_Disposition_View and read+edit in
            DPEG_Disposition_Edit in the same change."

        BOTH permission sets grant READ ONLY. DPEG_Disposition_View and DPEG_Disposition_Edit
        both carry `allowCreate`/`allowEdit`/`allowDelete` = false and `allowRead` = true on
        this object's objectPermissions block, and all eleven fields are `readable=true` with
        no field carrying `editable=true` in either set - measured by reading both
        .permissionset-meta.xml files directly, not assumed from their names. This is C3: the
        object is an append-only AUDIT TRAIL of who replaced a broker and when, written by
        `BovSubmissionService.replaceSelectedBroker` in SYSTEM_MODE (ARCHITECTURE.md §2
        automation-path exception - a write on the principal's behalf, not at their request),
        so no human persona - including one holding "Edit" in its permission set name - may
        rewrite it through the UI. `DPEG_Disposition_Edit`'s objectPermissions block is ALSO
        `allowCreate=false` here, same as `allowEdit`: every row on this object is written
        exclusively by `BovSubmissionService.replaceSelectedBroker`'s SYSTEM_MODE DML, never
        by a human clicking New, so there is no CREATE grant to preserve either. "Edit" in the
        permission set's name describes its role across the disposition module generally, not
        a promise about this specific object.
        This object, its fields, the layout, the compact layout, the list view and the two
        permission sets must land TOGETHER.

        🔴 SHARING: modelled on sharingRules/BOV_Submission__c.sharingRules-meta.xml - one
        sharingOwnerRules entry granting Edit to group DPEG_Acquisitions_Team from
        roleAndSubordinates Acquisitions_Analyst. See sharingRules/BOV_Broker_Change__c
        .sharingRules-meta.xml. Sharing rules deploy ONE AT A TIME in this org; do not batch
        this file's deploy with any other sharingRules file. DPEG_Acquisitions_Team was
        confirmed to exist in usman-dpeg before this file was written (queried live,
        DeveloperName='DPEG_Acquisitions_Team', Type=Regular, one row returned).
    -->
